Fuzix BASIC
===========

An integer BASIC in the spirit of ECMA-55 and TRS-80 Level II BASIC.

    basic            interactive
    basic prog.bas   load and run a program

Numbers are 16 bit integers (-32768 to 32767), strings up to 255
characters. Variable names start with a letter; the first two characters
count, as on the TRS-80. A$ is a string. Arrays come from DIM, or get
11 elements (0-10) when first used; one or two dimensions. True is -1.

Keywords must be separate words: FOR I=1 TO 10 (not FORI=1TO10). They may
be typed in lower case.

Commands:   RUN [line]  LIST [from][-to]  NEW  CLEAR  CONT
            SAVE "name"  LOAD "name"  (".bas" is added)  BYE / SYSTEM
            TRON / TROFF (trace line numbers)

Statements: LET  PRINT (or ?)  INPUT ["prompt";] var, ...
            IF expr THEN statements | line [ELSE statements | line]
            IF expr GOTO line
            FOR var = a TO b [STEP c] ... NEXT [var[, var]]
            GOTO  GOSUB  RETURN  ON expr GOTO|GOSUB line, ...
            DIM  READ  DATA  RESTORE  REM (or ')  END  STOP
            RANDOMIZE [seed]  CLS
            Several statements on a line are separated by ":".

PRINT:      ; joins, , goes to the next 16 column zone,
            TAB(n) and SPC(n) position.

Operators:  + - * / MOD  = <> < > <= >=  AND OR NOT (bitwise)
            + joins strings. &H1F is a hexadecimal constant.

Functions:  ABS SGN INT RND(n) (1 to n, RND(0) any)  LEN VAL ASC CHR$
            STR$ LEFT$ RIGHT$ MID$(s, start[, length]) INSTR(s, find)
            STRING$(n, char) POS(0) FRE(0)

Ctrl-C stops a running program; CONT goes on.

Memory: on the TRS-80 a program can use about 4K, the rest of the 32K
process holds the interpreter, the variables and the strings. FRE(0)
tells how much is left.
